1. DEFINITIONS

1.1. "Licensor" means the copyright owner or other person or entity
authorized to grant rights in the Software under this License.

1.2. "Contributor" means the Licensor and each person or entity that has
licensed a Contribution under this License and whose Contribution has been
incorporated into the Software.

1.3. "You" and "Your" mean the individual or legal entity exercising rights
under this License, together with entities that directly or indirectly control,
are controlled by, or are under common control with that legal entity. "Control"
means ownership of more than fifty percent of the voting interests or the legal
power to direct management.

1.4. "Software" means source code, object code, documentation, tests,
examples, build materials, configuration, and other materials included in a
release, branch, commit, package, repository snapshot, or copy to which this
License is expressly applied by a LICENSE file, package metadata, file header,
or other accompanying notice, excluding materials expressly identified as
being governed by another license.

1.5. "Source Form" means the preferred form for reading, understanding,
testing, and modifying the Software.

1.6. "Object Form" means any form produced by compilation, assembly,
linking, translation, packaging, code generation, or another mechanical
transformation of Source Form.

1.7. "Covered File" means a file in Source Form that is part of the Software
or that contains a substantial portion of code copied or translated from the
Software.

1.8. "Modification" means a change, addition, deletion, translation,
adaptation, or other alteration to a Covered File. A Covered File containing a
Modification is a "Modified Covered File."

1.9. "Corresponding Source" means:

(a) the Source Form of the Software and every Modified Covered File included
in a distributed Object Form;

(b) the build scripts, configuration, interface definitions, and other
materials reasonably necessary to build the covered portion of that Object
Form; and

(c) a clear description of the Modifications or a revision identifier from
which those Modifications can be determined.

Corresponding Source does not include source code belonging solely to a
Separate Work, credentials, cryptographic secrets, signing keys, customer data,
personal data, regulated data, or other information that is not reasonably
necessary to build the covered portion of the Object Form.

1.10. "Separate Work" means source code or separately compiled object code
that uses or communicates with the Software through public APIs, ABI
boundaries, function calls, static or dynamic linking, system calls,
command-line interfaces, network protocols, inter-process communication,
plug-in interfaces, or other defined interfaces, but does not contain a
substantial portion of the Software's implementation code.

Public declarations, function signatures, data types, constants, macros used
only to invoke public interfaces, and unmodified public headers do not by
themselves prevent a work from being a Separate Work.

1.11. "Larger Work" means a work that combines the Software with one or more
Separate Works.

1.12. "Distribute" means to sell, license, transfer, provide, publish, or
otherwise make a copy of the Software or an Object Form containing the Software
available outside Your legal entity.

Providing a copy to a contractor solely to perform services on Your behalf is
not Distribution when the contractor is bound to use it only for that purpose
and to protect non-public materials. You remain responsible for the
contractor's compliance.

Allowing users to interact with the Software solely over a network does not by
itself constitute Distribution.

1.13. "Commercial Use" means use of the Software, directly or indirectly:

(a) in production operations of a for-profit business;

(b) in, with, or for a paid product, subscription, hosted service, consulting
service, support service, or other offering provided for compensation;

(c) to generate revenue, materially reduce commercial operating costs, obtain
a commercial advantage, or directly support production business operations;

(d) for development, testing, integration, or research that directly supports
a then-current use described in paragraphs (a) through (c); or

(e) by or on behalf of a for-profit business after the Commercial Evaluation
period has expired, unless another express exclusion in this License applies.

Commercial Use does not include a Commercial Evaluation. Incidental donations
or reimbursement of actual costs to an individual, educational institution, or
nonprofit organization do not alone constitute Commercial Use.

1.14. "Commercial Evaluation" means non-production, internal evaluation,
testing, proof-of-concept work, or research performed solely to determine
whether to adopt the Software, during the ninety calendar days beginning on the
first day that You use the Software, provided that the Software is not used to
serve external users, generate revenue, materially reduce production operating
costs, or support production operations.

The Commercial Evaluation period is available only once to You, including all
entities treated as part of You under Section 1.3, and is not restarted by a new
release, branch, package, or Modification. The period ends immediately when any
use described in Section 1.13(a) through (d) begins. Any continued use described
in Section 1.13(e) is Commercial Use.

1.15. "Actual Knowledge" means knowledge acquired by You, if You are an
individual, or by one or more of Your employees, officers, or contractors who
are directly assigned to develop, integrate, test, secure, deploy, operate,
investigate, or maintain a system using the Software. Actual Knowledge requires
facts sufficient to form a reasonable technical suspicion. It does not include
constructive knowledge, rumors, or knowledge held solely by personnel unrelated
to the Software.

1.16. "Material Technical Impact" means one or more of the following occurring
in a configuration or use documented as supported, or, for paragraph (a),
reasonably capable of affecting supported use:

(a) unauthorized access, privilege escalation, memory corruption, information
disclosure, integrity loss, availability loss, security-boundary bypass,
capability or handle forgery, or another material security impact;

(b) memory-safety failure, data loss or corruption, a crash, deadlock, livelock,
persistent hang, or unbounded resource consumption that substantially
interrupts normal supported operation;

(c) materially incorrect task execution, scheduling, synchronization,
cancellation, timeout, channel, I/O, isolation, or portability behavior that
causes incorrect results or substantial operational disruption;

(d) a material violation of a documented public API or ABI contract that
causes incorrect results, interoperability failure, or substantial operational
disruption; or

(e) a repeated performance failure that materially impairs normal supported
production use and is demonstrated by controlled, materially comparable
measurements outside ordinary measurement variance or by violation of a
documented performance guarantee.

1.17. "Reportable Defect" means a good-faith and technically reasonable
suspicion, based on observed behavior, logs, test results, code inspection,
crash data, or reproducible conditions, that a defect originates wholly or
partly in the Software, has or creates a substantial risk of Material Technical
Impact, and either:

(a) is reproducible under conditions reasonably capable of being repeated; or

(b) is reasonably likely, based on the available technical evidence, to recur
or to affect users beyond Your specific environment.

A suspected Security Defect need not be reproduced when code inspection, crash
evidence, or observed behavior provides a reasonable technical basis for the
suspected security impact.

A Reportable Defect does not include a feature request, an immaterial cosmetic
issue, an immaterial documentation error, normal measurement variance, behavior
affecting only unsupported or experimental use, misuse contrary to documentation
that cannot reasonably affect supported users, behavior already documented as a
known limitation before You obtained Actual Knowledge, speculation without
technical evidence, a defect caused solely by a Separate Work, or a defect
caused solely by an unmodified third-party dependency.

1.18. "Security Defect" means a Reportable Defect involving an impact listed
in Section 1.16(a).

1.19. "Official Repository" means
https://github.com/Feralthedogg/LLAM or a successor location publicly
designated by the Licensor.

1.20. "Security Policy" means a file named SECURITY.md in the Official
Repository, or a successor security-reporting document publicly designated by
the Licensor.

1.21. "Reporting Channel" means:

(a) for a Security Defect, any usable private vulnerability-reporting feature
of the Official Repository, private reporting method designated in the Security
Policy, or private email address or other private contact method publicly
designated by the Licensor in the Official Repository, canonical project
website, or package metadata; and

(b) for any other Reportable Defect, the issue tracker of the Official
Repository, unless the Licensor publicly designates another reporting method.

1.22. "Report Materials" means technical descriptions, logs, reproduction
instructions, test cases, patches, samples, and other materials intentionally
submitted as part of a defect report.

1.23. "Contribution" means an original work of authorship intentionally
submitted to the Licensor for inclusion in the Software under Section 11. A
submission clearly marked "Not a Contribution" is not a Contribution.

