15. COMPLIANCE, TERMINATION, CURE, AND SURVIVAL

15.1. Rights granted under this License terminate automatically when You
materially violate its terms. A material violation of Section 8 terminates only
the copyright and patent rights granted under Sections 2 and 3 as exercised for
Commercial Use, including Distribution undertaken as part of that Commercial
Use. It does not by itself terminate rights exercised solely for noncommercial
use.

15.2. Except for termination under Section 13, Your terminated rights are
automatically reinstated if You fully cure the violation within thirty calendar
days after You first discover it or receive written notice identifying it with
reasonable specificity, whichever occurs first. Reinstatement does not erase
liability, if any, arising during the period of termination.

15.3. A failure to report under Section 8 is cured by submitting the required
report or by providing the Licensor a reasonable written explanation, supported
by the information then available, showing that the issue was not a Reportable
Defect, that no reporting duty arose, or that reporting was legally prohibited.

15.4. A copyright holder may extend a cure period or reinstate rights in
writing.

15.5. Termination does not terminate the rights of recipients who received the
Software from You. Each recipient's rights remain subject to that recipient's
own compliance with this License.

15.6. Termination does not end obligations that by their nature or express
terms apply after termination. Without limitation, the source-availability
commitments in Sections 5(d) and 5(e), Section 6.1(f), Section 6.2, and Section
6.3 for prior Distributions, any reporting duty that arose under Section 8
before termination, Sections 8.10 and 8.11, and Sections 9 and 12 through 19
survive termination.

15.7. The cure and reinstatement provisions of this Section do not restore a
patent license terminated under Section 13.

